@SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5000 
### Change to your host address ^

@token = YOUR_TOKEN
@repairVersion = 1
# Replace repairVersion with the latest version returned by GET before each change.



### Initial administrator: configure FirstAdmin in User Secrets (see README).

###=====================================List of Repair requests=====================================

### List of all repairs
GET {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Append new repair
POST {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "product": "Laptop",
  "isCustomProduct": false,
  "serialNumber": null,
  "description": "Broken screen",
  "reporterName": "Jan",
  "reporterSurname": "Kowalski",
  "reporterPhone": "123456789",
  "reporterEmail": "jan@example.com",
  "companyName": "Example",
  "companyAddress": "Example 1",
  "companyPostalCode": "00-001",
  "companyCity": "Warszawa",
  "companyNip": "5260250274",
  "hasWarranty": false,
  "hasContract": false,
  "serviceDataConsent": true,
  "marketingConsent": false
}


### assign the user to repair with id ...

POST {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs/18/take
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": {{repairVersion}} }


### complete the repair with id ...
POST {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs/18/complete
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": {{repairVersion}} }


### cancel the repair with id ...  for now users are able to discharge admins
POST {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs/21/cancel
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": {{repairVersion}} }


### return the repair with id ... for now users are able to discharge admins
POST {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs/22/return
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": {{repairVersion}} }


### Update repair with id ...
PUT {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs/17
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "product": "Laptop",
  "isCustomProduct": false,
  "serialNumber": null,
  "description": "Broken screen",
  "reporterName": "Jan",
  "reporterSurname": "Kowalski",
  "reporterPhone": "123456789",
  "reporterEmail": "jan@example.com",
  "companyName": "Example",
  "companyAddress": "Example 1",
  "companyPostalCode": "00-001",
  "companyCity": "Warszawa",
  "companyNip": "5260250274",
  "hasWarranty": false,
  "hasContract": false,
  "serviceDataConsent": true,
  "marketingConsent": false,
  "status": "Pending",
  "version": {{repairVersion}}
}

### Delete repair with id ...
DELETE {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs/20
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": {{repairVersion}} }


###=====================================List of User requests=====================================

### List of all users
GET {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/users
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Selected user
GET {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/users/17
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Logged user
GET {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/users/logged
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update user
PUT {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/users/13
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "Username": "jonh76",
    "email": "jonh67@example.com"
}

### Delete user - here for now
DELETE {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/users/9
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Edit user permissions 
# ===========================
# All of the permissions:
#         "ReadRepairs",
#         "TakeRepairs",
#         "EditRepairs",
#         "DeleteRepairs",
#         "ReadUsers",
#         "EditUsers",
#         "DeleteUsers",
#         "GrantUsers",
#         "DischargeUsers"
# ===========================
PUT {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/users/grant/17
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
{
    "permissionsGranted": [
       "GrantUsers",
        "ReadRepairs",
        "TakeRepairs",
        "EditRepairs",
        "DeleteRepairs",
        "ReadUsers",
        "EditUsers",
        "DeleteUsers",
        "DischargeUsers"
    ],
    "permissionsRevoked": [

    ]
}
###

###=====================================List of Authorization requests=====================================

### register user
POST {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "Mike2",
    "email": "Mike2@gmail.com",
    "password": "password123"
}

### login user
POST {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "UsernameOrEmail": "Mike1",
    "password": "password123"
}


### Customer repair lookup (use the code from the receipt)
POST {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs/check
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "ABCDEFGH", "email": "jan@example.com", "serialNumber": null }
